#{[{:db/doc "Requires identity, type, and a string value when explicitly ensured. The application checks supported answer types and field-scoped deduplication, keeps referenced values immutable, and may validate authored image availability. Do not reject an entered value solely because its math syntax is malformed." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045496 :db/ident :answer/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer/id :answer/type :answer/value]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, key, and type when explicitly ensured. The type-specific predicate validates owned answer values and canonical membership. Radio, select, blank, and checkbox require a nonempty bank and one canonical answer. Free permits an empty bank and no reference answer. Checkbox banks contain exactly two text answers, true and false. Writers also ensure answer/validate. Question field-key uniqueness, immutable referenced values, entered-answer reuse, and response completeness require application handling." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045491 :db/ident :answer-field/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer-field/id :answer-field/key :answer-field/type] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.answer-field/valid?]}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional reference to a question-generator entity holding a Python script that produces new questions for this KP. The application invokes the generator when more questions are needed, validates its output, and adds accepted questions to the KP's pool." :db/id #edb/ref 1040 :db/ident :knowledge-point/question-generator :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring KP identity, title, a canonical example question ref, and at least one practice question ref when explicitly ensured. Writers ensure question/validate for both examples and practice questions, along with child specifications. The application checks target types, nonempty canonical worked solutions, disjointness of all canonical targets from every practice pool, mathematical correctness, and selection rules." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045456 :db/ident :knowledge-point/validate :db.entity/attrs [:knowledge-point/canonical-example :knowledge-point/id :knowledge-point/questions :knowledge-point/title]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity and problem when explicitly ensured. The application requires complete answer fields before automatic grading, and a worked solution for canonical examples, validates any present fields and answer values, and derives example roles from knowledge-point/canonical-example and excludes those targets from every practice pool. A fieldless school problem may be displayed through assigned-problem without grading or awarding mastery." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045484 :db/ident :question/validate :db.entity/attrs [:question/id :question/problem]}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a validated question generator registered through knowledge-point/question-generator." :db/id #edb/ref 1169 :db/ident :question-generator/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Repository-relative path to the validated Python generator. Its package records supported templates, difficulty capabilities, finite limits, dependencies and reproducible CLI usage. Registration does not certify arbitrary generated output; generation must pass the content validation and durable commit workflow." :db/id #edb/ref 1168 :db/ident :question-generator/script :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}]}
